menu "Dummy remote options"

config PROVISIONING_HEADER_DIR
	string "Directory containing this unit's generated provisioning_data.h"
	help
	  Same option, same reasoning, as remote/Kconfig and dongle/Kconfig:
	  identity is baked into the image at build time by
	  dongle/tools/provision.py — PLAN.md §4.13. No default.
	  CMakeLists.txt FATAL_ERRORs at configure time if this is empty or
	  the file isn't there.

config REMOTE_TEST_RADIO_PROTO_MAJOR
	int "RR_IDENTITY radio_proto_major to report (bench test only)"
	default 2
	help
	  link.c (reused unchanged from remote/src/) references this symbol
	  directly — remote/Kconfig's own option, duplicated here rather than
	  shared, since Kconfig has no cross-application include mechanism.
	  Same default, same reasoning: A14 has no provisioning-record
	  representation, so this is the one deliberate build-time override,
	  defaulting to the real value (2 as of RADIO_PROTOCOL.md v2.0).

config REMOTE_DUMMY_STIM_INTERVAL_MS
	int "Self-stimulus press interval (ms)"
	default 3000
	help
	  PLAN.md §4.9: this board's job is to hold a connection, consume the
	  downlink, and generate uplink traffic at realistic rates — it does
	  not need a human pressing it. A synthetic press fires on this
	  interval through the identical gesture-classification path a real
	  GPIO edge would use, the same trick dongle/src/engine.c's TEST 2
	  plays for USB-side load. 3 s approximates a plausible referee
	  press cadence; lower it for W6/W7's density and load questions.

endmenu

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
